    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the primary statement line 'Total revenues and other income' is the sum of the three listed components. Each component is mapped individually as per the schema requirement.\n2. For total_operating_cost, the mapping follows standard practice for the oil & gas industry. It includes all operating expenses listed under 'Costs and other deductions' except for 'Interest expense' and 'Other taxes and duties'. 'Other taxes and duties' (e.g., production taxes, property taxes) are considered operating costs but are reported separately in the primary statement. The supplementary table indicates a portion is included in 'Production and manufacturing expenses' and 'SG&A expenses', but the primary statement total is used for the main cost lines. Therefore, 'Other taxes and duties' is not included in the mapped array as it is not broken out as a separate operating cost component in the primary list; it is a separate line item.\n3. For net_income, 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' is used, which is the bottom-line profit after all expenses, taxes, and noncontrolling interests.\n4. For taxes, 'Income tax expense (benefit)' is mapped directly.\n5. For interest_expenses, 'Interest expense' is mapped directly.\n6. The sign convention for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost follows rule 13: all values are positive as they reduce income.\n7. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of 'Other income', 'Depreciation and depletion', 'Other taxes and duties', and 'Income tax expense'), but the primary statement line items are used for mapping as they represent the consolidated totals.",
